The paper is correctly rejected; no generator is shipped.

The retained Track B prototype passed G1–G8, but failed mandatory G9(b):

- Easy: bare 0/3 solved; hinted 2/3.
- One permitted increase to medium: bare 0/3; hinted 1/3.
- The successful hinted answer passed exact verification.
- Mechanical recovery: 17,493 operations per instance.
- Compact route: 144 operations.
- Answer: 48 atoms, approximately 71 tokens.

Thus the rejection is based on demonstrated oracle performance, not merely the existence of an efficient algorithm. The paper’s theorem establishes worst-case NP-hardness, not hardness for this generated distribution. [Paper on arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.09835)

